{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1095093-the-i-want-to-do-every-damn-game-blues","id":1095093,"title":"The I want to do Every Damn Game Blues!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-05-21T05:36:24-07:00","id":1095093,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon8.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> The I want to do Every Damn Game Blues!","content":"So what the hell do you do when you just want to do all these different games... but hell you only have so much time?! There is never time/opportunity to make use of the Library of Groovy game?!<br /> <br /> I mean it took me this long to finally do a W20 game I've been chomping at since it came out! I am only able to maintain being a ST of two games Exalted 3rd, and W20 Wild West, but Hell I really want to do Changeling since it came out! And Mage when that came out... and a crazy crossover chronicle where everyone starts mortal/sorcerer/Psychics in the Dark Age setting and eventually everyone awakens and or embraced, and if they die they play wraiths!<br /> <br /> Or my Immortal Mariachi game, which I've been wanting to play since my old gaming group went to see Once Upon a Time in Mexico back in Highschool. Where everybody essentially plays an El Mariachi style secret Hitman with a gimicky weapon guitarcase. And are eventually cornered in a freaky ass Bar/Brothel ala Dusk Till Dawn. And at this point they are all dying, one becomes Embraced, One becomes possessed by a Fallen, One becomes a Highlander style Immortal, one Becomes a Mummy Style Immortal, ect...<br /> <br /> So what do you guys do when you want to play every game? Do you just go to your favorites? I mean my cases usually are my players are ignorant of the gamelines, but I put it to a vote, and two wanted Wild West Werewolves and everyone else was indecisive or voted something else.<br /> <br /> Do you resign yourself to the fate that you will never play certain games? I mean wow I like Wraith but it keeps being bumped lower on the queue, but this will certainly change with the Wr20 release. I've never had luck getting a Vampire game off the ground for instance. I mean it seems some groups really want to do it and others be like... &quot;umm being a blood rapist McSelfish corpse sounds sad&quot;. The positive spin I've done though would be you are playing people who got dealt a bad hand, whoops I'm a shovel head, so do you go with the wave and be evil (Sabbat), join the criminals who are the lesser evil (Camarilla/Anarchs), or go full off the Reservation Autarkis and become a Coterie of Vampire Hunters, or Golconda seekers.<br /> <br /> Sub Splats seem so cool but once again pushed down the queue, unless they are prologue games where your Mortals become vampires, or mages, or Wraiths.<br /> <br /> <br /> Then you have the crazy options like the Immortals in Mexico Game, where you have a story that can have a Crazy Crossover schtick going. But this has two varieties. Either everyone is specifically another splat, like say a PanFera Pack, or a Family where everyone becomes a different supernatural. Or a Game where its mostly one type of Supernatural who dominate the Themes but have familial or situational reason to have one or two tag alongs from another supernatural group. Like a Werewolf Pack with a Corax joining, or a Motley of Changelings with a Kinain Mage. Or a Coterie of Vampires with a Risen, Kueijin and or Ananansi joining along.<br /> <br /> This all can make your headspin when even one setting, the World of Darkness, has so much you want to play! I mean Ideally I can have all my various games in one setting thus getting maximum impact when a Wild West Group stumbles on a Viking Leech in a Coffin, and later you do a Dark Age Vampire game and its one of the NPCs or even PCs.<br /> <br /> <br /> All this in just one setting! It gets even sadder when you consider I also love the Chronicles of Darkness line and that is a whole different version of Earth!<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:22px\"><b>Whatcha Do?!</b></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-21T09:39:48-07:00","id":1095162,"title":"","content":"If you aren't afraid of learning the commands and using 20 year old tech, you might want to check the various mu*s on mudconnect.<br /> <br /> Most support player run plots (prp for short), and are starved for STs. Being willing and able to juggle multiple systems will make you popular quick.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5818,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","user":"EvilTyger","date":". 05-22-2017, 03:02 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}